    {
      "name": "typography",
      "type": "registry:item",
      "title": "Typography",
      "description": "Inter optical-sizing presets (opsz + letter-spacing per size × weight, including light 300/350), the semantic type scale (text-display … text-caption) as Tailwind v4 utilities, and per-family tracking/leading presets for Geist, Geist Mono, Montserrat, Lora, Source Code Pro, and Monaspace Neon.",
      "registryDependencies": [
        "dm-theme"
      ],
      "categories": [
        "foundations"
      ],
      "docs": "Import both stylesheets in your globals.css: @import \"../styles/typography.css\"; @import \"../styles/font-presets.css\". Load each family you use and expose it as --face-<id> (e.g. Inter({ subsets: [\"latin\"], axes: [\"opsz\"], variable: \"--face-inter\" })); the opsz axis is required for the Inter presets. Then point role aliases at families: --font-sans: var(--font-inter); --font-mono: var(--font-geist-mono); --font-heading: var(--font-montserrat); --font-serif: var(--font-lora).",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "styles/typography.css",
          "type": "registry:file",
          "target": "styles/typography.css"
        },
        {
          "path": "styles/font-presets.css",
          "type": "registry:file",
          "target": "styles/font-presets.css"
        }
      ]
    },
